A392 - Regarding some previously known philosophical concepts such as "do not steal" or "do not kill", it must be clarified that these are not absolute concepts but relative concepts. If a thief breaks a wall with a grating of a poor family to enter a house and steal some change, it is clear that it is a deplorable gesture, but if a very intelligent thief studying the security systems of a museum steals a work of art by overcoming very sophisticated security systems without breaking anything and gives it to a child in a kindergarten, so in this case "stealing" is actually a gesture that deserves respect, prestige and admiration. Similar reasoning can also be made for "not killing", given that I have written that reincarnation exists.